A||N||5||chris6878||Dash lights....  help..???||||5||
Z||000000||chris6878||10-31-2000||12:15 PM||||Hi all,<P>My fiero's dash lights use to work fine without any problems. Then they just stopped working. They use to work at random. Sometimes at night i would turn on my park lights and the guage lights would work. The next night it would be completely opposite..      <P>But they havent been working at all for the past 3-4 months, until last night. I went out to start her up and turned on the lights and boom, they guage lights came on fine for a bout 30 seconds and then went out again..<P>I have heard there is something under the dash that i can check that will cause this problem. It seems to be some type of loose connection or someting..               <P>could someone help me out?<BR>TIA,<BR>chris<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tigger||10-31-2000||01:11 PM||||Take the back cover off the instrument pod and check the bulbs.  You can remove the bulbs by turning the grey things on the backside a 1/4 turn and they will come out.  When you put them back, turn the plastic thing back and forth a couple times to make sure they have a good contact to the laminated circuits.<P>If this isn't the case, I'd check to make sure the two electrical plugs on both sides of the pod didn't come loose.  Hope this helps...<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||wwh0001||10-31-2000||01:32 PM||||<BR>Try this worked for me <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/techtips.htm#Dashlights" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/techtips.htm#Dashlights</A>  don't work?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||btoth||10-31-2000||01:49 PM||||my laminated circuit is worn away in some places so that the bulbs don't make contact... are the circuits still available or is there a way to repair them?||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||10-31-2000||08:31 PM||||there are repair kits for circuit boards that might work. try most any electronics supplier EXCEPT radish rack. radio shag doesn't have trace repair stuff.<P>That article of Paul Vargus' is way screwed up. I wish he'd fix it or remove it.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-31-2000).]||||reg||1
